00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.950
In the center of every galaxy is a supermassive black hole a black hole that can be

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.950
millions or billions of times the mass of our Sun that a kind of the most extreme object in the universe and

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.529
Sometimes they collide with each other

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.029
this is something unfortunately you'll never be able to see directly because they don't give out light that black holes, but

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:26.580
You can see them through the gravitational waves that they give out and in 2034

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:32.430
We'll be launching a spacecraft into space which will be a giant gravitational wave detector

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.210
It's called Lisa the laser

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:40.980
Interferometric space antenna and the facts around this mission are so cool and the stuff we'll be able to discover incredibly cool

